# RAII for temp dirs and processes

Own `QTemporaryDir` with `std::unique_ptr`. Resetting the pointer (or destroying the exporter) removes the directory via `QTemporaryDir`'s destructor. Do not `new`/`delete` it on every error path.

`QProcess` may stay parented to the `QObject`, but still discard the previous job before starting another (`disconnect`, kill, wait, `deleteLater`).

```cpp
// BAD
tempDir_ = new QTemporaryDir();
...
delete tempDir_;
tempDir_ = nullptr;

// GOOD
tempDir_ = std::make_unique<QTemporaryDir>();
if (!tempDir_->isValid()) {
    cleanup();  // tempDir_.reset()
    return;
}
```

Manual `cleanup()` should only reset smart pointers and clear related paths, not scatter `delete`.
